ContentScale.Crop

It scales the image so that it fills the entire area of the container (Box).

If the image’s aspect ratio doesn’t match the container, it crops the extra parts instead of leaving blank space.

Result: no empty space, the image completely covers the background.

Other common options:

Option	What it does
Fit	Scales image to fit inside container; may leave empty space
FillBounds	Stretches image to fill container, can distort it
Crop	Scales to fill and crops extra parts (keeps aspect ratio)
Inside	Scales down to fit inside without cropping